From: zerogap
Subject: keyboard: enable auto-repeat

Holding Backspace or an arrow key repeats it, as people expect. zerogap
tells repeats from real presses (src/kbdindev.cpp) and never lets a
repeat click a button.

diff --git a/lib/input/keyboardbehaviour.cpp b/lib/input/keyboardbehaviour.cpp
index d529c98..971323d 100644
--- a/lib/input/keyboardbehaviour.cpp
+++ b/lib/input/keyboardbehaviour.cpp
@@ -20,7 +20,7 @@
 #include <circle/input/keyboardbehaviour.h>
 #include <assert.h>
 
-//#define REPEAT_ENABLE
+#define REPEAT_ENABLE
 
 #define REPEAT_DELAY		MSEC2HZ (400)
 #define REPEAT_RATE		MSEC2HZ (80)
